<title>USA: McDermott probes centers on barge venture.</title>
<headline>McDermott probes centers on barge venture.</headline>
<dateline>NEW ORLEANS 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>J. Ray McDermott and its McDermott International Inc parent said on Tuesday that an audit of possible wrongdoing which could result in criminal and civil charges centers on possible anti-competitive activity at its heavy lift barge joint venture, HeereMac.</p>
<p>In July, McDermott International received an informal request from the Securities and Exchange Commission for the voluntary production of documents relating, in part, to HeereMac.</p>
<p>If the allegations are true, grand jury proceedings could result in civil and/or criminal liability for McDermott International and J. Ray McDermott. ((-- New York Newsroom 212 859 1902))</p>
</text>
